Title: Comprehensive Deep Learning Pipeline for Automated Skeletal Muscle Segmentation & Sarcopenia Detection on Abdominal CT

---

**1. Data & Cohorts**  
- Training: SAROS CT dataset, 550 scans/6516 slices.  
- Testing: 601 CT scans from SAROS, TCIA, WAW-TACE, In-house: acute pancreatitis, IBD, gallbladder cancer, bile duct obstruction.  

---

**2. Pipeline Stages**  
- L3 vertebra segmentation using TotalSegmentator  
- Automated L3 slice extraction  
- Skeletal muscle segmentation using nnU-Net  

---

**3. Evaluation Metrics**  
- Expert qualitative scoring  
- Dice coefficient  
- Intersection Over Union  
- Diagnostic accuracy for sarcopenia detection  

---

**4. Results**  
- Segmentation accuracy: Dice 0.93–0.97, IoU up to 0.94.  
- Expert: Vertebral segmentation 78–85% complete, muscle segmentation 90–92.6% excellent.  
- Sarcopenia: Sensitivity 0.94–0.97, Specificity 0.84–0.97, AUC up to 0.92.  

---

**5. Subgroup Analysis**  
- Consistent performance across disease conditions, CT protocols, contrast/non-contrast scans, radiation doses.  

